---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { SITE } from '../consts';
---
<Base
  title="Editorial Policy"
  description="Howloop's editorial standards for accuracy, independence, source verification, and correction handling across Australian financial guides."
>
  <div class="hl-wrap hl-prose-wrap">
    <article class="hl-prose">
      <h1>Editorial Policy</h1>
      <p>
        {SITE.name} publishes practical Australian financial calculators and plain-English guides. Because household money decisions require high trust, every guide and tool follows strict verification and independence rules.
      </p>

      <h2>1. Primary Source Verification</h2>
      <p>
        Tax thresholds, Superannuation Guarantee rates, HELP/HECS repayment tables, and Medicare rules are checked directly against statutory schedules published by the Australian Taxation Office (ATO), Services Australia, and Treasury. Banking product rates are sourced from the public Consumer Data Right (CDR) register.
      </p>

      <h2>2. Commercial Independence</h2>
      <p>
        We do not accept paid placements in our calculator results or bank rate tables. If display advertising is served via Google AdSense, advertisements are clearly labelled with an <code>Advertisement</code> header and have zero influence over which banking brands or rates appear in our tools.
      </p>

      <h2>3. Clear Separation of Base vs Bonus Rates</h2>
      <p>
        Our editorial policy prohibits combining conditional introductory or bonus interest rates into default long-term compound interest projections unless the conditions are explicitly disclosed.
      </p>

      <h2>4. Corrections &amp; Updates</h2>
      <p>
        When statutory thresholds change (such as annual July 1 tax and super updates) or a reader reports an error via <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a>, we verify the primary source, update the relevant calculator or guide, and log substantive changes on our <a href="/updates/">Updates</a> page.
      </p>
    </article>
  </div>
</Base>
